Create a sandbox, run one command in it, print a summary on stderr, and delete
the sandbox (also on error or Ctrl-C). anona-compute exits with the command's exit code;
-i/--stdin streams this terminal's stdin to the command.

Cost is printed when the API reports it; the current API does not, so the
summary says "unknown" rather than guessing.

Exit codes:
  0    success
  1    general error
  2    usage error (bad flag, argument or value)
  3    not signed in, or the credential was refused (HTTP 401/403)
  4    not found (HTTP 404)
  5    quota or rate limit (HTTP 429)
  exec and run pass the remote command's exit status through unchanged
  (0-255; 130 after Ctrl-C) and exit 125 when anona-compute itself failed,
  for any of the reasons 1-5 above; their --json error keeps that detailed
  code in "cli_code".

Usage:
  anona-compute run [flags] -- COMMAND [ARGS...]

Flags:
      --allow-out stringArray      host the sandbox may reach (repeatable); with --no-internet this is the allow-list
      --auto-pause                 pause instead of delete when the timeout ends
      --cmd-timeout duration       stop waiting for the command after this long (0 = no limit)
  -w, --cwd string                 working directory
  -e, --env stringArray            environment variable KEY=VALUE for the sandbox (repeatable)
  -h, --help                       help for run
      --idle-pause string          pause the sandbox after this long with nothing using it (e.g. 15m, 1h); "off" disables it. A duration also makes the timeout pause the sandbox instead of deleting it, as --auto-pause does
      --keep                       do not delete the sandbox after the command
      --metadata stringArray       metadata KEY=VALUE (repeatable)
      --name string                a name for the sandbox, shown beside its ID (stored as metadata name=NAME; the ID stays the identifier)
      --network-file string        JSON egress policy for the sandbox ("-" reads stdin); replaces the flags above
      --no-internet                create the sandbox without internet access
      --size string                sandbox size: small (1 vCPU, 2 GiB, 10 GB disk), medium (2, 4 GiB, 20 GB), large (4, 8 GiB, 40 GB) or xl (8, 16 GiB, 80 GB); default: the template's own size
  -i, --stdin                      send this terminal's stdin to the command (closed at EOF)
  -t, --template string            template ID or alias (default: profile default_template, else "base")
      --timeout string             sandbox lifetime before it is deleted or paused (e.g. 300s, 1h), or "never" for no time limit (default "300s")
  -u, --user string                user to run as (default: the sandbox's default user)
      --vault-inject stringArray   inject a vault secret into requests to a host: HOST:HEADER=[bearer:|basic:]SECRET (repeatable)

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output: one object per line on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
